  "description": "CALDID crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C39 H91 Eu5 O14. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.425-4.870 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.69-170.58°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu5O(OPrᶦ)13.",
